            <div xml:id="d1043">

                <pb facs="1039" n="1027" xml:id="pg1027"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.93114A/63: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Harrison</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-04-04T20:00:00-04:00">April 4, 1944—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1134. American Interests—China. With reference to your no. 1934 of March 30,
                    Department, in view of exceptional circumstances and as an emergency measure,
                    authorizes the expenditure for months of February, March, and April of
                    equivalent of not to exceed $110 monthly each to qualified internees and
                    non-internees as provided in Department’s 1011 of March 25. Please request Swiss
                    Government to make necessary financial arrangements on an urgent basis and to
                    ask Fontanel to begin payments immediately pending further consideration of
                    matter by the Department.</p>
                <p>Department urgently desires information as to “the restrictions or limitations
                    previously imposed” referred to in Section 2 of no. 1934 and advantages that
                    might be expected to accrue from their removal.</p>
                <p>Also please refer to your 1386, March 8, in connection with your 1934 and verify
                    number of interned and non-interned nationals and minimum monthly amount
                    necessary for financial assistance to each.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
